            "author": "Mark Webber",
            "status": "Published",
            "category_tag": "Support",
            "published_date": "2024-09-05",
            "detailed_content": "![](https://cdn.staging.oregon.platform-os.com/instances/11587/property_uploads/modules/insites_assets/assets_upload/asset/f2c89a69-c577-45c0-99dd-1db728a40e5d/stock-img10.webp?updated=1725522972)\n\n\n#### Develop user training materials:\n\n* Create user manuals, tutorials, and FAQs that cover the key features and functionality of the intranet.\n* Use clear and concise language that is easy for users to understand.\n* Include visual aids such as screenshots and diagrams.\n* Make the training materials accessible online or in printed format.\n\n#### Conduct regular training sessions:\n\n* Schedule training sessions for new users and refresher training for existing users.\n* Offer both in-person and online training options to accommodate different learning styles.\n* Provide hands-on training to allow users to practice using the intranet.\n\n#### Provide ongoing support through a help desk or ticketing system:\n\n* Establish a help desk or ticketing system to allow users to submit support requests.\n* Assign staff to respond to support requests in a timely manner.\n* Use knowledge base articles and FAQs to provide self-service support.\n\n#### Track and analyze user support requests:\n\n* Use a ticketing system to track and manage support requests.\n* Analyze support requests to identify common issues and areas for improvement.\n* Develop solutions to address recurring problems.\n\n#### Dependencies:\n* Intranet platform updates\n* Training materials\n* Help desk software\n\n#### Resources:\n* IT Help Desk\n* Intranet Administrator\n* Content Creators\n* Subject matter experts\n\nBy following these subtasks and addressing the dependencies, you can ensure that users have the knowledge and support they need to effectively use the intranet and maximize its benefits.",
